      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Results of industry-sponsored Phase III trials registered at clinicaltrials.gov include a rich amount of information on the efficacy of medical interventions. We propose that these results can be used to inform hypothesis testing of a new intervention through the Bayes principle. The posterior probability of positive efficacy offers an accessible interpretation of the uncertainty of efficacy and a convenient metric for global false-positive control."},
